{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1091501-umbra-w20-glens-give-you-super-healing-factors-now","id":1091501,"title":"Umbra W20: Glens give you Super Healing Factors now...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-12T05:59:39-07:00","id":1091501,"title":"Umbra W20: Glens give you Super Healing Factors now...","content":"Okay so I am reading the new Umbra book, and I am pretty pleased with a lot of the new facts and tweaks, like the idea echoes of Pollution don't usually cross the Gauntlet, and that Low gauntlet may feel like entering a nice hot tub and High Gauntlet is like jumping into a freezing lake.<br /> <br /> I am at a crossroads with the Glens though, they upgrade your healing... that is very potent... Garou already have insane healing, and here they can heal an aggravated wound a turn potentially... This makes me even more inclined to make them even rarer then ever before. Though its confusing since, Garou are like invincible gods there, so they would be easy to defend if they are there.<br /> <br /> And Gurahl can even have access to personal glens.<br /> <br /> That's a pretty big deal having these instant healing glens, it makes a lot of other healing magics obsolete if your Caern has one of these rare piles of purity tucked away.<br /> <br /> And Epiphs, I guess I always interpreted them as kind of dreamscapes, but wow they can be really nutzo, and maybe pocket dimensions of really out there ness.<br /> And Trods, so these intersect with the Dreaming yeah, because if Umbral Trods are different and far away from Dreaming Trods, well you wouldn't be stumbling into Faery parties, so it seems Trods exist adjacent to multiple realms of existence rather then them branching off and only pieces of them dipping into other realms?<br /> <br /> <br /> So its been out for a while, do you think its wise to just have Glens be this potent? Perhaps even require them to spend a Gnosis, or make a role to access the healing could curb some of the problem. Or maybe I am overthinking things and this is no problem?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:27:41-07:00","id":1091684,"title":"","content":"I feel like you're overthinking this. The Glen section provides plenty of drawbacks (even if narrative ones) for when hanging out in a Glen isn't a great idea. Glens are Wyld zones, and you can run into all sorts of issues just dealing with that unpredictability.<br /> <br /> As well... healing isn't exactly hard to come by in the game. I've had a PC that averaged healing ~5 Agg a turn using Mother's Touch alone in combat. Sure having one Garou focusing on healing instead of killing isn't always the best tactic but Garou don't need a Glen to recover from Agg very quickly. If you have a bunch of high-Rage characters that makes Mother's Touch hard, just make a bunch of Gaia's Breath talens instead.<br /> <br /> So sure, attacking the Garou protecting a Glen is hard because they'll superheal... but you can destroy a Glen without combat fairly easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 20